    "# Quiz: Introduction to Data Ethics\n",
    "\n",
    "> **On Alps:** These are the questions of this lesson's pre-lecture and post-lecture quizzes, from the course's quiz app, with the answers the quiz app accepts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pre-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-02-pre-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What is a consideration of ethics in Data Science?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Data collection</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Data collection is one area to check, but algorithm design is another.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Algorithm Design</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Algorithm design is one area to check, but data collection is another.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>All the above</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Ethics applies to both data collection and algorithm design.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-02-pre-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Which of the following are a part of ethical challenges?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Transparency</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Transparency is an ethics principle, a shared value. It is not one of the challenges.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Data privacy</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Data privacy is one of the ethics challenges, along with issues like data ownership.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Reliability and safety</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Reliability and safety is an ethics principle, a shared value. It is not one of the challenges.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-02-pre-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Data ethics also includes AI and machine learning algorithms</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>True</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Data ethics covers algorithms, including AI and machine learning.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>False, they are separate</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Data ethics studies algorithms too, including AI and machine learning.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Post-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-02-post-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What is the main difference between ethics and applied ethics?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Applied ethics is a specific type of ethics</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. That does not name the difference. Applied ethics is about finding ethical issues in real products and processes, then fixing them.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Applied ethics is not a real term</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Applied ethics is a real term. It means putting moral ideas into practice.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Applied ethics is the process of finding and correcting ethical issues</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Applied ethics means finding ethical issues in real products and processes, then fixing them.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-02-post-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What is the difference between ethics regulation vs ethics principles</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Ethics regulation focuses on regular ethics</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Regulations are laws, such as data protection laws, that organizations must follow.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>There is no difference</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Principles are shared values that people follow by choice. Regulations are laws.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Ethics principles do not relate to a particular law, while regulations do</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Ethics principles are shared values, not laws. Regulations are laws that must be followed.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-02-post-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Which of these are real ethical principles and practices that can be applied?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Collection bias</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Checking data for collection bias is one practice. Following data protection laws is another.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Compliance with ethics regulations</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Following data protection laws is one practice. Checking data for collection bias is another.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>both of the above</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Both apply: checking data for collection bias, and following data protection laws.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  }
